{
  "Song of Songs.5.16.4-t.html": "<html>\n<header profile=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/11/profile\" > \n        <meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/> \n        <title>Song of Songs 5:16.4</title>\n</header>\n    \n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n        <h1>Song of Songs 5:16.4</h1>\n        <h4>Based on color photos, the dagesh in the het is an anomaly.</h4>\n        \n        <table align=\"center\"><tr><td>\n            <img src=\"../../Changes/2021.10.19 - Changes/images/2021.05.26/1-Detail.jpg\" border=\"4pt\"/>\n        </td></tr>\n        <p/>\n        <tr><td>\n            <center><i>Credit: Sefaria.org.\n            </i></center>\n        </td></tr></table>\n        <p/>\n        The dagesh in the het has a reddish color and is slightly larger than normal.\n        <p/>\n        <b><i>Ben Denckla</i></b>\n        <p align=\"right\"><b>2021.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2021.05.26-1</b></p>\n        <p/>\n        <table border=\"1pt\" align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"16pt\">\n            <tr><td>\n              <span style=\"color:blue;font-size:14pt\">\n                  <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?t\">All \"Transcription uncertain\" ('t') notes</a>\n              </span>\n              <p/>\n              <span style=\"color:blue;font-size:14pt\">\n                  <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n              </span>\n            </td?</tr>\n        </table>\n        <p/>\n        </body>\n</html>\n",
  "Song of Songs.6.8.3-c.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2023.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2023.09.11, number: 3 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Song_of_Songs 6:8.3</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Song_of_Songs 6:8.3</h1>\n  <h2>Consider dagesh in mem. Add note 'c'.</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2023.10.19 - Changes/images/2023.09.11/3-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>The dagesh in the mem is slightly reddish and slightly over-sized, but well-positioned.</p>\n  <p>BHL has no dagesh in the mem.  BHLA has a dagesh in the mem.</p>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Daniel Holman</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2023.10.19 - Changes/2023.10.19 - Changes.xml?2023.09.11-3\">2023.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2023.09.11-3</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?c\">All \"Text is correct relative to LC. Usually this marks a peculiarity of the LC relative to the other Masoretic texts.\" ('c') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Song of Songs.7.13.4-c.html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\"><HTML>\n<!-- \n     Computer generated from NoteMaker[20 Jan 2026]: \n     Changes file: 2021.10.19 - Changes.xml, date: 2021.08.07, number: 18 .\n     Remove this token \"****COMPUTER-GENERATED****\" if you edit this file manually.\n-->\n<head><meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/>\n  <title>Song_of_Songs 7:13.4</title>\n</head>\n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n  <h1>Song_of_Songs 7:13.4</h1>\n  <h2>Word lacks accent, add note 'c'; MAM ends the word with a Maqaf (  ס־  ).</h2>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"5pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>\n          <img src=\"../../Changes/2021.10.19 - Changes/images/2021.08.07/18-Detail.jpg\"  border=\"4pt\">\n          </img>\n        </center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <center>Credit: Sefaria.org.</center>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n  <p>\n    <b>\n      <i>Ben Denckla</i>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <p align=\"right\">\n    <b><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Changes/2021.10.19 - Changes/2021.10.19 - Changes.xml?2021.08.07-18\">2021.10.19 - Changes.xml : 2021.08.07-18</a>\n    </b>\n  </p>\n  <table align=\"center\"  cellpadding=\"20pt\"  border=\"1pt\">\n    <tr>\n      <td>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?c\">All \"Text is correct relative to LC. Usually this marks a peculiarity of the LC relative to the other Masoretic texts.\" ('c') notes</a></center>\n        </p>\n        <p>\n          <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n        </p>\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </table>\n</body></HTML>",
  "Song of Songs.8.12.1-t.html": "<html>\n<header profile=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/11/profile\" > \n        <meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\"/> \n        <title>Song of Songs 8:12.1</title>\n</header>\n    \n<body background=\"../../Images/Background\">\n        <h1>Song of Songs 8:12.1</h1>\n        <h4>Based on color photos, the accent on the kaf should be a patah, not a qamatz.</h4>\n        \n        <table align=\"center\"><tr><td>\n            <img src=\"../../Changes/2021.04.01 - Changes/images/2020.10.27/1-Detail.jpg\" border=\"4pt\"/>\n        </td></tr></table>\n        <p/>\n        A qamats on the kaf is generally accepted as anomalous spelling. \n        However, viewed in black and white facsimiles\n            it is distinct and well-formed.\n        <p/>\n        The color facsimile provided by the author (above) \n            shows the qamatz dot has a different color from the qamatz bar \n            and is possibly an artifact.\n        The folio page has a large splash mark in the center \n            and the dot in the qamatz may be the result of a sub-droplet of the splash.\n        The dot is also to the left of the center of the patah bar \n            in contrast with dots on most other qamatzs on the page.\n        <p/>\n        If the dot does not represent scribal intent, the qamats becomes a patah as shown in the UXLC.\n        <p/>\n        <b><i>Alexander Adler</i></b>\n        <p align=\"right\">27 October 2020</p>\n        <p/>\n        <table border=\"1pt\" align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"16pt\">\n            <tr><td>\n              <span style=\"color:blue;font-size:14pt\">\n                  <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml?t\">All \"Transcription uncertain\" ('t') notes</a>\n              </span>\n              <p/>\n              <span style=\"color:blue;font-size:14pt\">\n                  <center><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"../../Supplements/Notes.xml\">Note index</a></center>\n              </span>\n            </td?</tr>\n        </table>\n        <p/>\n        </body>\n</html>\n"
}
